<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top</id><updated>2026-11-22T16:28:44Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-top" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Israel's Eisenkot condemns 'Jewish terrorism' in West Bank</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0f4ce47cc69913b43c2116c6fa7cfd91db1526e770428dfa38f91da254d34d62</id><updated>2026-11-22T16:28:20Z</updated><published>2026-11-22T15:09:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/israel-s-eisenkot-condemns-jewish-terrorism-in-west-bank/a-80013861--f4c08d0b63d1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/israel-s-eisenkot-condemns-jewish-terrorism-in-west-bank/a-80013861?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Israeli opposition leader Gadi Eisenkot has condemned a recent series of arson attacks in the occupied West Bank as "Jewish terrorism." Israeli authorities have opened an investigation into the incidents.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>COP31 climate talks end without consensus on how to fund vulnerable countries or move the world away from coal, oil and gas use</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:66d1b9c76ca7b4f29f5427d364dc29128f927d96ba0218b2519d83d6a2ca0524</id><updated>2026-11-22T16:28:23Z</updated><published>2026-11-22T13:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/cop31-climate-talks-end-without-consensus-on-how-to-fund-vulnerable-countries-or-move-the-world-away/a-80003610--d912dc284aaa.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/cop31-climate-talks-end-without-consensus-on-how-to-fund-vulnerable-countries-or-move-the-world-away-from-coal-oil-and-gas-use/a-80003610?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">After two weeks of tough talks, the COP31 climate summit has closed without a consensus on how to quit fossil fuels or fund countries struggling to adapt to a hotter world.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>COP31: Climate deal 'not adopted,' summit president says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:db368272f761f530843b5ebf30aec9886dbb75893b5375c9d66e7eca1a1d802c</id><updated>2026-11-22T16:28:26Z</updated><published>2026-11-22T12:39:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/cop31-climate-deal-not-adopted-summit-president-says/live-79999516--d760f7d7f78d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/cop31-climate-deal-not-adopted-summit-president-says/live-79999516?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The summit was extended as nations worked to reach a deal, but they couldn't agree on including fossil fuels. European nations, small island states and activists have criticized oil-producing countries for the impasse.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Bayern Munich bosses under fire over Jamal Musiala comments</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c5b57167d7e95e42bfd97a7a9eba8c8f6e837fee7f60a0def2e2171a59f58e1e</id><updated>2026-11-22T16:28:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-22T11:30:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bayern-munich-bosses-under-fire-over-jamal-musiala-comments/a-80013187--78383bcfae5b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bayern-munich-bosses-under-fire-over-jamal-musiala-comments/a-80013187?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Officials have publicly questioned whether Musiala will ever fully recover from a debilitating neurological condition and queried the validity of his contract, prompting criticism from fans, media and the FIFPRO union.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>China, ASEAN countries struggle over South China Sea code of conduct</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:22c2770fafd2037ff5d408a912ea7d91b1169ec221830c4bfb00893ac2c308cf</id><updated>2026-11-22T16:28:31Z</updated><published>2026-11-22T08:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/china-asean-countries-struggle-over-south-china-sea-code-of-conduct/a-80009799--a3492edf3810.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/china-asean-countries-struggle-over-south-china-sea-code-of-conduct/a-80009799?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Philippines wanted a South China Sea code of conduct in place by 2026. But persistent disagreements between China and ASEAN countries are slowing progress toward a deal.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Inspired by Bernie Sanders: A German agency is using US-Style campaigning to boost the left in 2029</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2ed3952987dfd45f4c42d48d309d00d3f58fe16b8c310542bd62485d8fdf49f9</id><updated>2026-11-22T16:28:34Z</updated><published>2026-11-22T08:39:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/inspired-by-bernie-sanders-a-german-agency-is-using-us-style-campaigning-to-boost-the-left-in-2029/a-80001443--f6cd4061ee72.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/inspired-by-bernie-sanders-a-german-agency-is-using-us-style-campaigning-to-boost-the-left-in-2029/a-80001443?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">"The Goodforces" wants to see a swing to the left in the 2029 German elections. The agency counts New York Mayor Zohran Mamdani and Bernie Sanders among its inspirations. Could it transform the political landscape?</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: IG Metall union calls for new 24-hour strike</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f5878253fc19e881f6c2b7f8fcca58aecddb295d8e1ce970bc8c675dce69fc0b</id><updated>2026-11-22T16:28:38Z</updated><published>2026-11-22T08:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-ig-metall-union-calls-for-new-24-hour-strike/live-80008430--32c896775229.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-ig-metall-union-calls-for-new-24-hour-strike/live-80008430?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany's biggest single union, IG Metall, is calling on car and shipyard workers to strike amid a pay row. Meanwhile, Germany's president is setting off on an Africa trip. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>US: ICE arrests 2 at Seattle airport in 'chilling' scenes — governor</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:95d6507e5f8be8fce8b362f6dc920fde8483e5946c0f32700fb1f8cc7335030c</id><updated>2026-11-22T16:28:40Z</updated><published>2026-11-22T07:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-ice-arrests-2-at-seattle-airport-in-chilling-scenes-governor/a-80012480--94de32aa4552.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-ice-arrests-2-at-seattle-airport-in-chilling-scenes-governor/a-80012480?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Washington's governor has denounced the arrests made by ICE officers at Seattle's airport, calling the incident "horrific."</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>India: Nepal PM Balendra Shah heads to Delhi for first bilateral visit</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:15c1c0cc24d80c50ba98bc6a2653e6ab1a63cbd58cf9558a2d69f3d92026275b</id><updated>2026-11-22T16:28:44Z</updated><published>2026-11-22T07:20:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-nepal-pm-balendra-shah-heads-to-delhi-for-first-bilateral-visit/live-80008104--4f17524b4e9e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-nepal-pm-balendra-shah-heads-to-delhi-for-first-bilateral-visit/live-80008104?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Nepal's rapper-turned-prime minister Balendra Shah is in New Delhi for his first foreign bilateral trip since taking office. He is expected to discuss flood recovery, trade and energy in his talks with Modi. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Dozens missing as deadly fire hits Indonesian candy factory</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:69d326ab4b775ba9815f395c51006d11cf21e0ea99b8233d451027263e30ce7a</id><updated>2026-11-22T16:27:22Z</updated><published>2026-11-22T06:14:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/dozens-missing-as-deadly-fire-hits-indonesian-candy-factory/a-80012342--07c7cd5dbdea.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/dozens-missing-as-deadly-fire-hits-indonesian-candy-factory/a-80012342?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">At least three people were killed in a devastating fire at a confectionery factory on Java. Officials said many more people remain unaccounted for, prompting fears of a much larger tragedy.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Nigeria: At least 24 dead after boat capsizes</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:45ae1ae95177391562feb89745a30173b128bf61ee4cca9bf1c0aca690c345e4</id><updated>2026-11-22T16:27:22Z</updated><published>2026-11-21T23:52:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nigeria-at-least-24-dead-after-boat-capsizes/a-80011248--a7e001c6016b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nigeria-at-least-24-dead-after-boat-capsizes/a-80011248?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The boat carrying mourners for a funeral overturned in southern Nigeria. It was the latest in a series of deadly boat accidents in the country.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Getting rid of antibiotic resistance: Challenges and possible solutions</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ca4103c41abad6e15e4dc4183966e0b086582eea2972dd59c16f4793ee9d1836</id><updated>2026-11-22T16:27:22Z</updated><published>2026-11-21T18:39:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/getting-rid-of-antibiotic-resistance-challenges-and-possible-solutions/a-80010693--ca5fce49b0a7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/getting-rid-of-antibiotic-resistance-challenges-and-possible-solutions/a-80010693?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">If antibiotics stop working, even the smallest infection can be fatal. The WHO expects millions of deaths over the next 25 years. Can the "One Health" approach help combat antibiotic resistance?</summary><category term="NRS-Import" /></entry><entry><title>Mexican special forces arrest drug kingpin 'Chapo Isidro'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:544b6ac6336c1a1ebe4b9afeead6a9e836e0c75463ded30dfc070bdce94236e3</id><updated>2026-11-22T16:27:22Z</updated><published>2026-11-21T18:30:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/mexican-special-forces-arrest-drug-kingpin-chapo-isidro/a-80010745--0adb20796144.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/mexican-special-forces-arrest-drug-kingpin-chapo-isidro/a-80010745?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The alleged leader of the Beltran Leyva gang and one of the FBI's most wanted fugitives, known as "Chapo Isidro," was captured by the Mexican military following a raid and a shootout in the coastal state of Sinaloa.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Russian helicopter suspected of violating Finnish airspace</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6f373695d51b010644daefd08952e13f1b42d8d12cbdb2cf5943f31d0e3e23e5</id><updated>2026-11-22T16:27:22Z</updated><published>2026-11-21T17:08:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/russian-helicopter-suspected-of-violating-finnish-airspace/a-80010133--74b233a91706.html" type="text/html"